    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced a gross back year release of GBP 22.0m in 2021, primarily driven by favorable claims development across various lines of business. This included a GBP 5.6m gross release from long-tail casualty classes, a GBP 10.0m gross release from the short-tail account (likely property), and a GBP 6.4m gross release from continued improvement on the large Irish motor account (2012-2016 underwriting years). Modest reserves were retained for older events like the Japanese earthquake and Thai floods (2010/11), and ultimate gross loss estimates for Superstorm Sandy were reduced. The ultimate gross provision for Covid-19 (2020 event) also saw a reduction. Overall, prior year development was favorable, contributing to a positive run-off.",
